      "instructions": "---\nname: bily-local-auth\ndescription: Local auth workflow for https://local.bily.ai:3000 using the Chrome plugin (no passwords in tool logs). Use whenever testing Bily authenticated flows locally, especially if login appears stuck.\n---\n\n# Bily Local Auth\n\nNever type or paste passwords through Codex tools. Tool calls are logged.\n\nFor any interactive testing, always use the Chrome plugin (`@Chrome`) so you get the real user session and extensions.\n\n## Open the app in Chrome\n\n1. Use `@Chrome` to open `https://local.bily.ai:3000`.\n2. If you land on `/login`, ask the user to sign in manually in Chrome (do not type credentials via tools).\n3. Continue testing in the same Chrome tab/window so the session is reused.\n\n## Verify session (API signal)\n\n```bash\ncurl -k -sS https://local.bily.ai:3000/api/auth/get-session | jq -r '.user.email // empty'\n```\n\nExpected: the curl command prints an email, and Chrome reaches the authenticated app without manual login prompts.\n",
