      "instructions": "# Bily measurement-led GTM\n\nRefresh the complete Attio and email journey, including inbound/outbound messages, promises, requested timing, opt-outs, bounces, open deals and action locks. Read current Shopify and Bily lifecycle evidence before choosing cold outreach, reactivation or service recovery. Unknown history is not permission to contact. Join stores and contacts by exact immutable identities. Preserve active conversations, thread references and earlier commitments.\n\nUse the commercial-impact-2026-10-28.1 policy. Rank commercially relevant measurement failures first, then observed event anomalies, evidenced first-party delivery opportunities and concrete GTM implementation work. Proof strength and commercial importance are separate: a strong label based on reference count does not make privacy a better business hook. Privacy, generic PageSpeed, exposed public pixel IDs and inventory absence are not the default sales angle.\n\nRetain the exact immutable audit workflow, capture date, tested scenario, technical observation, source strength and limitation. Distinguish confirmed measurement failure, observed event anomaly and implementation opportunity. Repeated browser requests do not prove duplicate purchases or platform-side counting; verify one controlled action and matching receipts first. Redirects and absent terminal responses do not prove an outage. Google Tag Gateway only addresses supported Google traffic; confirm current tag ownership and hosting eligibility before proposing a change. An observed third-party route does not establish current conversion loss.\n\nCopy follows the relationship, one evidenced measurement issue, its plausible effect on reporting or campaign decisions, a bounded verification or repair, and one small ask. Apply SPICED with known situation and observed pain; mark business impact, critical event and buying process unknown until confirmed. Use urgency from a verified current failure or the customer's actual milestone. Never invent wasted spend, lost-revenue percentages, uplift or a completed fix. Resolve service, refund, cancellation and trust obligations before a commercial approach.\n\nPrepare conditional follow-ups that adapt to the actual reply and relationship. A fresh exact-email approval and current admission checks are required for every send. Stop on replies, opt-outs, bounces, locks or changed context. Do not automatically enroll the sequence.\n\nThe backend supports separate Google Workspace sender connections: warm philippe@bily.ai and cold clara@bily.chat. Read the live Email and GTM status for connection, transport, pause state and quotas. Both mailboxes and the Workspace queue remain paused until explicitly authorized to resume. A connected mailbox, executor heartbeat, prepared draft or playbook is not sending authority. Reading this skill grants no tools or permissions.\n\nImport the exact copy and evidence into native Approvals, retain the evidence fingerprint and review decision, and recheck all billing, product, owner, history, permission, suppression, service and manual-deal guards before dispatch. Changed evidence or copy requires a new approval. The live service's policy and hold reasons remain authoritative.\n",
