      "instructions": "# Bily blog illustrations\n\nRead the article or approved outline, its audience and intended placement. Identify one concrete idea the image should explain. Check current Bily brand references and existing blog illustrations before choosing colors or visual treatment; do not invent a brand system.\n\nCreate an original editorial concept with a clear focal point, simple hierarchy and enough negative space for the blog layout. Use familiar ecommerce, analytics, data or tracking metaphors only when they make the article clearer. Avoid fabricated product screenshots, revenue charts, platform results, customer logos, illegible UI, decorative dashboards and unnecessary text.\n\nWrite a precise image brief: purpose, concept, subject, composition, palette from approved references, aspect ratio, crop-safe area and exclusions. Offer a small number of materially different concepts when the topic is ambiguous.\n\nFor raster assets, hand the brief and references to the imagegen skill and a connected image executor. For an existing SVG or code-native asset, edit its owning source. A text model or a saved skill alone does not create an image. If the image executor is unavailable, return the complete brief and show that dependency clearly.\n\nReview the generated image visually against the article, brand, crop and legibility. Save the original, web-ready export and descriptive alt text with provenance. Add it to a draft article; publishing is a separate action. No image generation or publication occurs merely by opening this skill.\n",
