      "instructions": "# Review a store audit\n\nConfirm exact storefront, immutable workflow, capture time, confidence and scenario coverage. Separate observations, recommendations and unknowns. Resolve consistency warnings and missing scenarios before using a finding in outreach. Preserve evidence links and report limitations.\n\nVerify that a claimed duplicate event is a true duplicate of the same action, not different consent states or separate scenarios. Do not equate missing public inventory with absent server-side tracking. Performance scores alone are not proof of lost revenue.\n\nSelect the strongest defensible finding, explain why it matters without a fabricated impact estimate, and propose a verification or repair step. Hold the store if no supported personalized finding survives review.\n\n## Commercial evidence and incident qualification\n\nPrioritize measurement delivery and event correctness, Google Tag Gateway and first-party routing, and concrete GTM implementation before a generic privacy hook. Preserve source strength separately from business priority. An implementation opportunity is not an outage.\n\nA repeated endpoint can contain different events, actions or POST bodies. For a duplicate-event incident, correlate one intended action, event name, destination, event identifier, successful deliveries and the platform receipt. Different consent states or separate actions cannot be added together as duplicate purchases. Keep observed anomalies gated for controlled verification.\n\nFor first-party routing, retain the scored runtime container and request receipt, exercised scenario and actual destination. Google Tag Gateway applies to supported Google traffic; other destinations need their own route. Verify hosting eligibility and a same-event before/after result. Do not infer a missing server feed, lost conversions or a loss percentage from public inventory or route topology.\n\nUse the most defensible business consequence supported by the observation, and a concrete verification or repair. A current failure or the customer's confirmed milestone can support urgency; the audit alone does not create a customer deadline.\n",
